WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:36.850
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.420
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.970
Haga and Ryuzaki!

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:39.140
You're blaming Yugi and me for your failures?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:43.660
That's why you sold your souls to Doma?

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.750
Sorry, but we can't lose against you!

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.020
Not until we crush Doma!

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.970
But I'm worried about Yugi.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:56.600
Can he duel when he hasn't recovered from his shock?

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:02.600
Timaeus Fails to Activate

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:15.610
My turn!  I draw!

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.620
I flip over my trap!

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:19.980
I activate Natural Selection!

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:20.990
What?

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.660
This trap can only activate during your turn.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:29.180
I select your monster, and it creates a monster with the same power.

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.000
And your original monster is destroyed.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:33.230
What?

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.330
I select Insect Queen!

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.310
How dare you do that to my Queen!

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:53.950
Just watch!  I tribute my Insect Token!

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.620
I summon Armored Centipede!

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.870
Take this!

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:04.930
Armored Centipede attacks Kuriboh!

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:17.480
Armored Centipede gains 500 attack points every time it destroys your Insect-Type monster!

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.680
I end my turn.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:31.200
The monster created by Natural Selection disappears at the end of his turn.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:38.160
Once again, I only have an infected Obnoxious Celtic Guard.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.200
Here I go.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.810
Tyrant Dragon, crush Red-Eyes!

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.620
Red-Eyes...

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:03.290
Whoa!  It's too early to sleep, Red-Eyes.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:06.930
I flip over my trap, Chain of the Underworld!

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:13.430
What?  Red-Eyes is back?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.260
Chain of the Underworld activates when your monster is destroyed.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:23.940
It Special Summons the destroyed monster, but with 700 fewer attack points.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.950
What are you planning, Ryuzaki?

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.420
Why would he revive a monster he destroyed?

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.220
You don't know why, Jonouchi?

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.360
Tyrant Dragon can attack twice during a single Battle Phase.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:43.310
But only when you have a monster on your field.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.760
What?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:50.900
You resurrected Red-Eyes so that you can destroy it again?

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.900
Yeah!  Red-Eyes betrayed me!

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:56.010
I haven't forgiven it!

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.140
C'mon!  Draw!

00:04:58.550 --> 00:04:59.640
Draw?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.000
When Chain of the Underworld activates, you can draw a card.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.300
Hurry up and draw.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:09.750
Ryuzaki, you'd go that far?

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:14.990
That's how you treat Red-Eyes?

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.730
It's all your fault, Jonouchi!

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:23.340
Tyrant Dragon, destroy Red-Eyes again!

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.600
I won't let you!

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.470
I flip over my trap, Celebration of Creation!

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.350
You idiot!  Traps don't affect Tyrant Dragon!

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.580
I never said I'm using it on Tyrant Dragon!

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:52.480
When an effect Special Summons a monster, this card ends your turn!

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:55.600
Ryuzaki, your Battle Phase is over!

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.200
What?

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:02.210
Red-Eyes, I won't let you go to the graveyard again!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.230
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:19.090
It's finally time!

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:22.260
The third turn of Parasite Caterpillar's effect!

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:24.840
Obnoxious Celtic Guard is destroyed.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.830
And Poison Butterfly hatches!

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:45.660
Jonouchi, you only have 300 life points.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.650
There's nothing you can do to win.

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.280
You don't know that until it's over!

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.160
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:56.760
Here I go!

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:59.280
I summon Gearfried the Iron Knight!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.930
And I activate my spell card!

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.590
Pot of Greed!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.510
I draw two cards from my deck!

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.350
Do you know this, Ryuzaki?

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:27.080
Long ago, there was a swordmaster with no equal in the world of Duel Monsters.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:38.490
With a single slash, he slashed the sea, split the sky and broke the earth.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:44.440
After facing his sword, no one returned alive.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:55.050
Fearing his own strength, the swordmaster chained himself and sealed his sword forever.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.550
That seal will now be removed!

00:07:58.500 --> 00:08:01.580
I activate my spell card, Release Restraint!

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:07.870
Remove your restraints and appear, Gearfried the Swordmaster!

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:17.800
What?  Only 2600 attack points?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.540
Stop bluffing!

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.950
You drew Claw of Hermos?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:37.680
Yugi, as long as Poison Butterfly is on your field, you take 500 damage every turn.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.890
What's with him?

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.740
Did you draw that card?

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.560
Like I thought.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:57.110
Damn!  I can't believe he drew his key card now!

00:08:57.110 --> 00:08:58.930
It's over, Haga!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.850
I will end this duel!

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:04.120
I activate Eye of Timaeus!

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:14.200
It combines with Poison Butterfly to summon a new monster-

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:19.670
Timaeus?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:22.170
Why doesn't it activate?

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.600
Don't scare me like that, Yugi.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:32.100
Did Timaeus abandon me?

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.420
What's going on?

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.640
The card abandoned you!  How pathetic!

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.400
I wouldn't be able to stomach it!

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.860
I'd be too ashamed to call myself a duelist!

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.160
Knock it off!

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:50.350
I end...

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:52.870
I end my turn.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.120
Did you say "end?"

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.870
That means Poison Butterfly's effect activates.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.480
You lose 500 life points.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.260
Yugi has 700 life points.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:09.720
At this rate, the other Yugi will lose his soul!

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:12.720
Yugi, you're finished.

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:14.960
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:20.020
I set a card and end my turn.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:34.310
Claw of Hermos combines with a monster on the field to transform into an Equip Card.

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.410
Prepare yourself, Ryuzaki!

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.680
I activate Claw of Hermos!

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:44.620
Swordmaster, I'll give you the ultimate sword!

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:57.200
I equip Gearfried the Swordmaster with Red-Eyes Black Dragon Sword!

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:01.200
The equipped monster gains 1000 attack points!

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:05.940
And 500 attack points for every Dragon-Type monster!

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:10.950
What?  There's only one Dragon-Type: my Tyrant Dragon!

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:14.660
So it gains 1500 attack points!

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:18.960
Gearfried the Swordmaster has 4100 attack points!

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.460
No way!  It'll destroy my Tyrant Dragon!

00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:27.200
When Gearfried the Swordmaster is equipped with an Equip Card...

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:31.470
...its effect activates and destroys your monster!

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:35.200
Tyrant Dragon is destroyed!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:40.220
No way!  Since it was an effect instead of an attack...

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:47.220
Ryuzaki, you've lost your soul before.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.520
But you returned to normal.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:54.320
So there must be a way to save you.

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.330
Wait, Jonouchi!

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:04.180
I must defeat you to save you!

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:07.320
Here I go!  Gearfried the Swordmaster attacks!

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.370
Attack Ryuzaki directly!

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:12.910
Dark Mega Slash!

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:18.280
Save me!

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.570
Sorry, Ryuzaki.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:55.040
Ryuzaki!

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:57.580
Pull yourself together, Ryuzaki!

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:02.820
Did you really lose your soul?

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:06.790
I promise to retrieve his soul!

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:09.330
It's Doma who can't be forgiven!

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.800
They play with people's lives!

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:13.580
Jonouchi...

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:17.760
Pegasus, Yugi...  I'll save them all.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:20.040
Including Mai.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.650
Just wait, Doma!

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:24.880
I'll never forgive you!

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:28.320
I'll crush you!

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.820
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:34.510
It's no use.  You've already lost.

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:36.820
The king doesn't know when to give up.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:39.600
I'll never give up.

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.290
Not until I save my partner!

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:44.830
I summon Breaker the Magical Warrior!

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:51.180
I activate my trap card!

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.430
Infestation!

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.940
All monsters lose 100 attack points.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:07.750
And we take 100 points of damage for every monster on our field.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.340
I win, Yugi!

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.540
You only have 500 life points.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:23.200
When this turn ends, Poison Butterfly's effect lowers your life points to 0.  The end.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.310
Yugi!

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:32.310
Stay there and watch him lose, Anzu.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:35.450
Hey, Yugi.

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:41.320
I promised to tell you your partner's location if you won, right?

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.770
But I won't need to tell you because you're going to lose.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.180
How dare you!

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.220
But I'm actually nice.

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:57.640
So I'll tell you because I feel bad for you.

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:01.140
I saw it.

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:07.510
I saw the card where your partner - the other Yugi's soul - was sealed.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:12.750
Where is it?  Tell me!

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.820
Be patient.  Calm down.

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:24.000
This is the card.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:26.500
What?  Give it to me!

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:28.870
Should I?

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.870
Fine.  I feel bad, so you can have it.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:36.720
I changed my mind!  Naturally!

00:15:36.720 --> 00:15:40.770
We're in the middle of a duel.  Hurry up and make a move!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:51.220
Unbelievable!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.730
Haga!

00:15:53.730 --> 00:15:55.150
Just kidding!

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:56.730
I lied.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:58.970
This was a regular card.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.970
You're the worst!

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.200
It was a joke.

00:16:05.160 --> 00:16:07.940
Prepare yourself, you bug!

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:19.950
I activate Breaker the Magical Warrior's effect!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.450
Mana Break!

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.870
Breaker the Magical Warrior's effect?

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:31.700
No way!

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:40.440
By removing a Spell Counter, Breaker the Magical Warrior destroys a spell or trap card!

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:46.290
Destroy Insect Barrier, Breaker the Magical Warrior!!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:56.580
This effect can only be used once per Spell Counter.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:17:04.610
After activating this effect, Breaker loses its Spell Counter and 300 attack points.

00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:09.700
But I can use the Poison Butterfly you gave me to attack you!

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.740
Here I go, you bug!

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:16.450
Poison Butterfly attacks Armored Centipede!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.430
I'm not done!

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:28.690
Breaker the Magical Warrior attacks you directly!

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:36.100
Just kidding!

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:39.800
All your monsters have finished attacking.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:43.160
Due to Poison Butterfly's effect, you'll have 0 life points!

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:47.110
All right!  I win!

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:49.340
You're mistaken.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.560
My Battle Phase isn't over yet!

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:59.080
Nonsense!  All your monsters have finished attacking!

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:03.520
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Berserker Soul!

00:18:03.860 --> 00:18:05.890
Berserker Soul?

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.390
I discard my entire hand to activate its effect!

00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:17.640
I can keep drawing and discarding from my deck until I draw a non-monster card.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:23.640
Every time I discard, my monster with 1500 or lower attack points can attack again!

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.650
1500 or lower attack points?

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:30.850
Back then...

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:44.600
After activating this effect, Breaker loses its Spell Counter and 300 attack points.

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.930
Yugi had this planned?

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.530
Here I go!

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:52.080
I draw the first card!

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:53.910
It's a monster card!

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.810
I discard Queen's Knight!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:01.220
Breaker the Magical Warrior can attack again!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.720
I draw my second card!

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.450
It's a monster card!

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.300
The third card!

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:19.260
It's a monster card!

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:23.640
I draw a monster card!

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:27.710
I draw a monster card!

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:31.980
I draw a monster card!

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.380
I draw a monster card!

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.360
I draw a monster ca-

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:46.630
That's enough, Yugi!

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:48.860
Let me go!

00:19:48.860 --> 00:19:51.380
Haga already has 0 life points!

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:53.510
The duel is over!

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.440
It's fine.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:24.430
By battling the legendary dragons' chosen duelists, their souls are stronger.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:29.070
They're valuable sacrifices for our god's resurrection.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.280
Haga!  I won!

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:37.810
You promised!  Tell me!

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.810
Where's my partner?

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.660
Tell me!  You promised!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.920
Where's my partner?

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.150
Where is he?  Answer me!

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:50.540
It's no good.

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.830
You know that, Yugi.

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:55.660
They already took Haga's soul.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:58.010
Haga!

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:03.000
Haga never could've kept his promise!

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:07.420
Tell me!  Where's my partner?

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:09.240
Poor Yugi.

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:12.740
Partner...

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.250
Yugi...

00:21:24.950 --> 00:21:26.260
Yugi!

00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:08.350
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:16.760
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:27.850
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:37.370
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:46.400
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:47.180 --> 00:22:51.910
I'll live feeling them

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:57.090
For me to be me

00:22:57.090 --> 00:23:05.550
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:11.190
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:20.920
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:30.420
Yugi defeated Haga, but he hasn't escaped the darkness in his heart.

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:35.170
But the train derailed and fell into a deep valley.

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:38.590
We're still alive?

00:23:38.590 --> 00:23:43.920
We were rescued by an old man and a girl who protect the valley.

00:23:43.920 --> 00:23:46.550
Who are these people?

00:23:46.550 --> 00:23:49.370
Why do they know Yugi?

00:23:49.370 --> 00:23:52.370
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Battle!  Two Yugis

00:23:52.370 --> 00:23:54.350
Duel, standby!
